      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=EX5-063#qaResult_card",
        "num": 2,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for EX5-063 (Sep. 13, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it activates.",
        "question": "Does \"then, delete 1 of your opponent’s lowest level Digimon\" in this card's [On Play][When Digivolving] effect activate even if my opponent doesn't have as many or more total Digimon and Tamers as me?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can.  The 2nd [All Turns] effect on EX1-073 [Machinedramon] can interrupt both deletions performed by this card's [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect.",
        "question": "I play this card when my opponent only has 1 EX1-073 [Machinedramon] in the battle area. At this time, I use \"delete 1 of your opponent's highest level Digimon\" in this card's [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect, and the 2nd [All Turns] effect on my opponent's EX1-073 [Machinedramon] interrupts it and prevents the deletion.  If I then use this card's \"delete 1 of your opponent's lowest level Digimon\" effect, can the 2nd [All Turns] effect on my opponent's EX1-073 [Machinedramon] again interrupt the effect?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
